Use a simple workflow for routine tasks or customer-facing processes when:

  • It’s easy to automate;
  • You have limited control over the process;
  • The task is repetitive or time-consuming;
  • You want human oversight without requiring high accuracy.
For example, use a simple workflow with clear steps and expected outcomes—such as sending emails by email or retrieving sales data from a database—instead of an AI agent that can handle complex queries or large volumes.
